  <h2>2. Eligibility</h2>
  <p>You must be at least 18 years old and able to form a binding contract to buy a membership.</p>

  <h2>3. What a membership is, and what it is not</h2>
  <p>
    A membership is an annual, recurring subscription giving you access to the automation packs,
    the weekly Security Watch briefs, and, on the higher tier, the Academy courses. Current tiers
    and prices are shown on the <a href="/">membership page</a> and are the only prices that apply.
  </p>
  <p>
    A membership is <strong>not</strong> a consulting engagement, a managed service, or support for
    your estate. Nobody from OraDiscuss connects to your systems, reviews your configuration, or is
    on call for you. There is no service level agreement of any kind, and none is implied by the
    price. What stands in place of one is a public changelog and email support on the material
    itself.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Everything sold is read-only</h2>
  <p>
    This is the core of what OraDiscuss sells and the reason the rest of these Terms can be short.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Nothing we sell modifies your database.</strong> The scripts collect and report. They
      issue no DDL and no DML against your data. Where a pack offers an optional local history
      table for trend projection, it is a separate, clearly marked file that you choose to run
      yourself, it is never invoked automatically, and every pack works fully without it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No verdicts, no commands.</strong> Reports state what your database recorded. They do
      not tell you what to do, and they do not emit commands for you to paste. Interpretation and
      any action remain entirely yours.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Source-visible.</strong> Every script ships as readable source so you or your security
      team can inspect it before it runs. We expect you to.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Local collection.</strong> Diagnostic packs run on your machine and write their output
      on your machine. Nothing is transmitted to OraDiscuss, and we never receive your estate data.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Your responsibility before running anything</h2>
  <p>
    You are the DBA. You are responsible for reviewing any script before you run it, for running it
